# Build Bible V2 — Chapter 12 (Enterprise FastSpring Billing)

Spec: `docs/14_BUILD_BIBLE_V2_CHAPTER_12_PADDLE_BILLING.md` (content superseded by FastSpring cutover; Paddle sections are historical-only)

## Rules

- FastSpring is the sole active billing provider and Merchant of Record (`getActiveBillingProvider()` → `"fastspring"`).
- Entitlements resolve only via `resolveOrganizationEntitlements` after verified sync.
- Never grant access from browser checkout success callbacks.
- Webhooks: verify signature, enforce idempotency, fail safely, never corrupt billing state.
- Emit commercial analytics only through `trackBillingLifecycleEvent` without org/customer IDs.
- Keep secrets server-only (`FASTSPRING_API_USERNAME`, `FASTSPRING_API_PASSWORD`, `FASTSPRING_WEBHOOK_SECRET`).
- Do not reintroduce Paddle or Stripe as an active checkout/portal path — legacy Paddle code/data stays historical-only.
- Do not change auth, RBAC, RLS, SEO, accessibility, or analytics architecture outside billing hooks.

## This chapter

- Do not commit, push, or deploy from Chapter 12 work.
